<title>USA: CBS-TV upfront ad market edges up - source.</title>
<headline>CBS-TV upfront ad market edges up - source.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Westinghouse Electric Corp's CBS Television Network sold about $1.25 billion in upfront advertising for the coming fall primetime TV season, up about $100 million from last year, according to a senior CBS executive.</p>
<p>After adding sales during its coverage of the Nagano Winter Olympics next year, advertising sales totalled $1.8 billion, said the executive, who declined to be identified.</p>
<p>&quot;It was an extremely fine upfront selling season,&quot; the executive said.  CBS was able to increase its cost-per-thousand ad rates 11-12 percent.</p>
</text>
